# 不是本仓库的 GitHub-Release 归档；快照内容、校验和与复算入口见 README
# 与 INVENTORY.md。
message: >-
  If you use AITester in your research, please cite this software.
# 2026-10-16 定位对齐（R2/R26 叙事重构的漏网点）：标题不再以 multi-agent
# 为主表述——完整编排臂相对轻量检出优先协议净负（−28pp，ADR-0016），
# 多智能体编排在本项目中定位为可消融容器（非主断言）。
title: AITester — Detection-First Python Test Generation and Repair Evaluation (Attribution) System
authors:
  # ORCID pending / ORCID 待补充：现有作者条目为集体署名
  # （AITester Contributors），无个人 ORCID iD 可填；CFF 1.2.0 的 orcid 字段
  # 需真实 ORCID iD（形如 0000-0000-0000-000X），不得以占位值填入，故此处
  # 仅登记待补充项。[待补充：作者 ORCID iD（如需按个人署名提交）]
  - name: AITester Contributors
    website: https://github.com/1956178912/AITester
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24136905
repository-code: https://github.com/1956178912/AITester
abstract: >-
  A Python system for attribution-aware evaluation of LLM-based unit test
  generation and repair, regenerated end-to-end on a single-provider corpus
  (DeepSeek), with the detection-first protocol ("red before
  green") as the primary success criterion, SpecIR specification oracles,
  paired attribution baselines (plain_llm / plain_llm_df), and M1 honest
  metrics (detection / repair / false-fix) adjudicated by held-out gold
  materials. Multi-agent orchestration is included as an ablatable container
  (not a primary claim: the full orchestration arm is net-negative versus the
  detection-first prompt protocol, ADR-0016). The accompanying evaluation
  methodology — pooled multi-seed statistics with McNemar, Bayesian paired
  analysis, BH-FDR, Wilson intervals, effect sizes, and template-cluster
  sensitivity — is an integral part of the artifact.
keywords:
  - software testing
  - LLM agents
  - unit test generation
  - automated program repair
  - fault detection
  - specification mining
